{"title":"Career Roadmap · CT/MRI Technologist","role":"CT/MRI Technologist","summary":"A CT/MRI Technologist is an allied-health imaging professional who operates CT and MRI systems, prepares patients, follows imaging protocols, positions patients correctly, maintains safety standards, performs image-quality checks, and supports radiologists in producing diagnostic-quality images.","facts":{"Current degree":"Allied Health Sciences (B.Sc / BPT / BOT / BMLT etc.)","Course":"Radiology & Imaging Technology"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A CT/MRI Technologist is an allied-health imaging professional who operates CT and MRI systems, prepares patients, follows imaging protocols, positions patients correctly, maintains safety standards, performs image-quality checks, and supports radiologists in producing diagnostic-quality images."},{"type":"p","text":"The role combines:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Radiographic and imaging principles"},{"text":"Human anatomy and physiology"},{"text":"CT technology"},{"text":"MRI technology"},{"text":"Patient positioning and communication"},{"text":"Radiation and MRI safety"},{"text":"Contrast-media procedures"},{"text":"Image-quality optimization"},{"text":"PACS/RIS and digital healthcare systems"},{"text":"Emergency response and infection control"}]},{"type":"note","label":"Important","text":"CT and MRI practice is generally built on a recognized radiology/imaging technology qualification and supervised clinical training. Exact eligibility, registration, scope of practice, and title requirements can vary by institution, employer, and applicable Indian regulatory requirements."}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"flow","items":["UG / Imaging Technology Degree","Clinical Radiology Training","X-Ray / CT / MRI Fundamentals","Clinical Internship","Radiology Technologist / Imaging Technologist","CT Technologist /